    Present only in the `plus` flavor: :app attaches this module through plusImplementation, so
    the core APK does not contain this manifest, this service, or any of the code behind it.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <application>

        <!--
            android:process=":assist" is the whole point of this module existing separately.

            A quantised 1-3B parameter model is hundreds of megabytes resident. Loading one into
            the IME process would make the process that every other app types through into the
            largest thing on the device, and the memory killer sorts by exactly that: the
            keyboard would be reclaimed while backgrounded and pay a cold start on the next tap
            in any text field. In its own process the model is loaded on an explicit user
            action, released after ninety seconds of inactivity, and the process it lived in can
            be killed at any moment without the keyboard noticing.

            exported="false": bound only from within this application, over an explicit
            component name. Nothing outside the app can reach the assistant, and the assistant
            reaches nothing outside - there is no network in this process either.
        -->
        <service
            android:name="com.borderkeys.assist.TextAssistService"
            android:process=":assist"
            android:exported="false" />

    </application>

</manifest>
